+The [post-commit diagnosis](results/20261003-post-commit-diagnosis/report.md)
+examines the committed runtime with fresh stage measurements, an inspection
+hashing control and a borrowed identity-serialization candidate. All 330 exports
+and 35 selected Anki checks passed. Serial inspection was slower; the identity
+candidate remains experimental because its overall timing and RSS evidence did
+not establish a reliable benefit. Production code remains at `eb4b463`.
+
+The [optimization-path exploration](results/20261003-optimization-paths/report.md)
+isolates nine candidates and tests a combined identity/SQLite candidate. All
+690 diagnostic exports and 74 selected Anki checks passed; separate duplicate-byte
+and ID microbenchmarks are retained with their narrower scope. Borrowed identity,
+ID derivation and SQLite connection reuse reduce local work, but combined export
+timing remains inconclusive. Thread, PNG and memory-digest controls did not show
+a reliable general improvement. Production code and the formal matrix are unchanged.
+
+The [structural dataflow experiments](results/20261003-structural-dataflow/report.md)
+remove an unused native legacy mirror, move temporary HTML ownership, reuse local
+card plans and omit an unconsumed native package fingerprint. All 460 exports and
+49 selected Anki checks passed; a separate 16-export Cloze workload passed raw and
+semantic checks without Anki. Uninstrumented confirmation shows about 2.2–4.4 MiB
+paired RSS savings on standard profiles and 43.3 MiB on wide text. Standard timing
+intervals still cross zero; wide text shows a roughly 36.2 ms paired saving.
+Candidates remain experimental; production and the historical matrix are unchanged.
+
+The [production structural rerun](results/20261003-structural-genanki/report.md)
+implements those four dataflow changes with no public API changes or experimental
+switches. Its single complete matrix retains 840 validated exports, 40 actual Anki
+checks and 10 timings/5 independent RSS samples per implementation/cell. All 20
+Rust timing medians remain above Sep 21; at 1,000 notes they are 7.3–19.9% higher.
+Independent RSS at 1,000 notes is 8.1–9.7% lower than the preceding implementation's
+archive. These are separate sessions; the report does not attribute their full
+differences to code. Sources, the uncommitted patch, regression evidence and offline
+replay are retained.
+
+The [five-direction exploration](results/20261003-next-directions/report.md)
+tests isolated staging omission, collection-to-ZIP streaming, Node project COW,
+prepared candidate reuse and early duplicate-byte lookup against same-executable
+controls. All 576 formal artifacts and 44 selected Anki checks passed, with 433
+Rust library tests. No-change compare-then-publish reuse reduced total medians
+36.3–46.6%; Node improved synchronous submission latency, wide fields benefited
+from staging omission, and repeated large bytes benefited from early lookup.
+Collection-only ZIP streaming had no established speed benefit. The report keeps
+paired uncertainty, independent RSS regressions, preparation failures, complete
+sources and replayable records. These candidates remain isolated from production.
+
